What this fork does
-------------------

It turns a retired COLDCARD Mk4 into a virtual pet ("Tamagotchi"). The
creature lives on the microSD card, ages only while the device is
powered, and can die. The pet code is in `shared/pet_*.py` and is
described in README.md.

Firmware built from this tree is signed with the PUBLIC developer key
(key zero, `stm32/keys/00.pem`). The COLDCARD bootloader detects this
and shows a large warning plus a forced delay on every boot. That is
expected. It also means anyone can build this; nothing here is genuine
Coinkite firmware.

